  "asr_text": "The personality trait they focused on was conscientiousness, the tendency to work seriously and steadily. Their analysis found that, within the same person, higher income was linked to higher conscientiousness later on. Wait, we thought this was about personality affecting income, but income got a part too, and the arrow doesn't point just one way. A rise in conscientiousness was also weakly linked to higher income later on. They found a weak connection not only between personality and later income, but also between income and later personality. Hearing this, it's tempting to ask, so does a pay raise update your personality too? But hold on, before reaching that conclusion, this was an analysis of data that tracked changes, and it cannot prove that income changed personality or that personality increased income. Something else may have affected both.",
